# Extracted data and anything derived from it is NOT committed by default.
#
# These directories hold material from two different provenances, and only one
# of them is cleared for redistribution:
#
#   PUBLIC  - derived from the ENWRA/LPSNRD public release (see PROVENANCE.md)
#   PRIVATE - derived from the Aarhus Workbench exports delivered by Ted Asch,
#             pending his permission
#
# Derivatives inherit the provenance of their source: a line shapefile built
# from Ted's inversion export still carries his line geometry, so shp/ is
# ignored on the same terms as data/.
#
# Ignoring these means a stray `git add -A` cannot publish the private half.
# Add cleared files deliberately with `git add -f <path>`.
#
# This matters more than usual here: the repo is private now and will be
# flipped public, and flipping publishes the whole history, not just the
# current tree.
data/
shp/

# python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# scratch extracts kept out of the way
data/_working/
